--TEST--
`throw` refuses an operand that no `catch` could match — a string here, and by the same rule any class outside the standard library's § 10 tree
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `nvs_ir::lower::exception` builds a landing pad against that tree and lowers
// no other shape, so the checker refuses the operand rather than leaving the
// lowerer to meet it.
string $reason = "the disk went away";
throw $reason;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0780]: `throw` takes a `Throwable`, and `string` is not one
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
